**Dirty Pipe (CVE-2022-0847)** is a vulnerability in the Linux kernel (versions **5.8+**) that allows an unprivileged user to **overwrite data in read-only files**, including **SU binary, `/etc/passwd`, and other critical system files**. This can lead to **local privilege escalation (LPE)**.

